---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Pricing — CanYouDo?">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <p class="kicker">Pricing</p>
      <h1>One rate. Fully transparent. No surprises.</h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--ink-600)">Every clean costs <strong>£20 per hour</strong>. Here's exactly where it goes:</p>

      <div class="price-split" style="margin:30px 0" role="img" aria-label="£15 to the cleaner, £5 to CanYouDo">
        <div class="part worker"><span class="amount">£15/hr</span><span class="who">paid directly to your cleaner</span></div>
        <div class="part platform"><span class="amount">£5/hr</span><span class="who">introduction fee</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>£15/hour — the cleaner's money</h3>
          <p>Paid by you, directly to your cleaner, on the day (bank transfer or cash — their payment details are shown on your confirmed booking). We never touch it, and we never take commission from it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>£5/hour — the introduction fee</h3>
          <p>Paid online when you book. It funds the booking system, automatic emails and reminders, messaging, the ratings system, customer support — and the monthly bonus pot that rewards outstanding cleaners.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top:52px">The bonus pot</h2>
      <p>Part of every introduction fee is set aside to reward measurably excellent work. Each calendar month, a cleaner with at least 4 completed and rated bookings can earn:</p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Bonus</th><th>The measure</th><th>Amount</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Punctuality</strong></td><td>On time for 100% of rated visits</td><td>£20</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Completion</strong></td><td>Cleaned all requested areas on 95%+ of visits</td><td>£20</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Excellence</strong></td><td>Average overall rating of 4.5★ or higher</td><td>£10</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="hint" style="margin-top:10px">Up to £50/month, paid by CanYouDo? on top of hourly earnings. Because ratings are factual (on time — yes or no?), bonuses reward what customers actually experience.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:52px">What customers provide</h2>
      <p>You supply all cleaning products and equipment (vacuum, mop, sprays, cloths). Your home, your products, your standards — and it means your cleaner isn't hauling supplies between jobs or passing that cost back to you.</p>

      <div class="notice notice-info" style="margin-top:34px">
        <strong>Example:</strong> a 3-hour weekly clean costs £60 — £45 straight to your cleaner, £15 introduction fee. A great cleaner doing 20 hours a week through CanYouDo? earns £300/week plus up to £50/month in bonuses.
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top:30px"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/find-a-cleaner/">Find a cleaner</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
